{"parentUuid":"4651076e-34be-441a-99a7-9a745d6145a5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9d21fbe7-2171-490f-98bf-e68d230dd581","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"can you take a look at the changes and this comment: Built-in help command invisible to pre-Execute Find check\n\nLow Severity\n\nrootCmd.Find(args) is called before rootCmd.ExecuteContext, but Cobra lazily initializes certain built-in commands (notably help and completion) during Execute via InitDefaultHelpCmd. The custom help command set via SetHelpCommand in NewRootCmd is stored on the struct but not added to the command tree until InitDefaultHelpCmd runs. This means Find([\"help\"]) pre-Execute won't find the help command, so resolvePlugin could dispatch to an entire-help binary on PATH instead of showing built-in help — violating the \"built-ins always win\" invariant."},"uuid":"a185220c-0c74-4c70-a3a9-ff9624601f56","timestamp":"2026-05-06T12:57:52.777Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"d3f01bb0-fb75-46a6-ae70-8aab0a703055","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
