{"parentUuid":"3ee0f913-79e2-43c1-b2cb-9fa7965c56c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01U1MDJvdbm416PEMCP7y2j2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both basically pass the parent environment through unfiltered — and neither treats env scrubbing as a security boundary, because plugins live on `$PATH` and are inherently trusted to run as the user.\n\n**kubectl** (`pkg/kubectl/cmd/plugin/plugin.go`):\n- Inherits the full parent environment via `os.Environ()`. No scrubbing.\n- Adds a couple of plumbing vars (historically `KUBECTL_PLUGINS_CALLER`, now mostly removed; `KUBECTL_COMMAND_HEADERS` for telemetry).\n- Auth specifically: nothing is *pushed* — kubectl relies on `KUBECONFIG` (a path) being inherited, and the plugin reads/parses it itself (usually via client-go). The token never lives in an env var that kubectl owns.\n\n**gh CLI** (`pkg/cmd/extension/manager.go`):\n- Same: full environment inherited.\n- Pushes a small set of namespaced vars: `GH_HOST`, `GH_REPO`, `GH_PATH` (back-pointer to the gh binary), and the existing `GH_TOKEN` / `GITHUB_TOKEN` if set.\n- Auth pattern: extensions are expected to **call back** (`gh auth token`, `gh api ...`) rather than read a token from env. The parent CLI is the source of truth for credentials; the extension pulls on demand.\n\n**The interesting design choice for us**, if `ENTIRE_AUTH_TOKEN` ever exists:\n\n| Approach | Pros | Cons |\n|---|---|---|\n| Push (env passthrough, current) | Zero plumbing; works offline | Every plugin sees the token even if it doesn't need auth; refresh is messy |\n| Pull (plugin calls `entire auth token`) | Least-privilege — only plugins that actually call get it; centralizes refresh; auditable | Plumbing — you have to expose `ENTIRE_PATH` (back-pointer) so plugins can find the parent reliably |\n\ngh's pull-based flow is the more defensible default if/when we add auth. Neither kubectl nor gh tries to defend against a *malicious* plugin via env scrubbing — that's not the threat model. The boundary is \"did you install this on your PATH.\"\n\nOne small thing we already do that aligns with gh: we inject `ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION` and `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` (`plugin.go:155-158`). If we go the pull route later, adding `ENTIRE_PATH=os.Args[0]` (resolved) is the natural next step so plugins can `exec $ENTIRE_PATH auth token` without hardcoding paths."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":99032,"output_tokens":2342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2342,"cache_read_input_tokens":99032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamURQhmtn9Xct9fukYor","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e265a32-a277-41ba-bb29-9228fbb17d3e","timestamp":"2026-05-06T14:29:29.247Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"d3f01bb0-fb75-46a6-ae70-8aab0a703055","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
