{"parentUuid":"0e4c66b7-96b0-4e1d-b7c9-2fae5309faeb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"34ee74a9-1d3d-47dc-95e4-d303a635b660","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Ok, but let's say we want to be better, should we add an allow list of variables we path through? Like \"PATH\" or the one relevant for CI / TTY checks, and in general anything that is common in an ENV and then filter out anything else for now? Can you make a suggestion?"},"uuid":"3f5821e9-e87b-453b-b4cb-55b76738e1fb","timestamp":"2026-05-06T15:47:06.389Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"d3f01bb0-fb75-46a6-ae70-8aab0a703055","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
{"parentUuid":"3f5821e9-e87b-453b-b4cb-55b76738e1fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JEXvEMPJ67U6NGsEk3i27b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101759,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5722,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101759,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":5722,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101759},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamaPgsFzPY2Tkzf1z6Dr","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e40e59c-2f57-45cb-9787-e7f8b50e6b36","timestamp":"2026-05-06T15:48:06.996Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"d3f01bb0-fb75-46a6-ae70-8aab0a703055","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
{"parentUuid":"5e40e59c-2f57-45cb-9787-e7f8b50e6b36","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JEXvEMPJ67U6NGsEk3i27b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good instinct — defense in depth here is cheap. Let me sketch what I'd actually ship.\n\n## Proposal\n\nA **prefix + exact-match allowlist**, with one opt-out env var for users who need more. Build it in a single helper called from `runPlugin`:\n\n```go\n// pluginEnv builds the child environment from the parent. We allowlist a\n// small set of OS-plumbing and TUI-detection variables that virtually every\n// program needs, plus prefixes we own (ENTIRE_*) or that are well-defined\n// passthrough namespaces (LC_*, XDG_*). Anything else — credentials,\n// tool-specific config, dev-loop debug flags — is dropped.\n//\n// Escape hatch: ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV=\"AWS_*,GIT_*,FOO\" lets the user opt\n// individual names or wildcard prefixes back in.\nfunc pluginEnv(parent []string, extra ...string) []string { ... }\n```\n\n## The list\n\n```go\n// Exact names (case-insensitive on Windows).\nvar pluginEnvAllowed = map[string]struct{}{\n    // POSIX basics\n    \"PATH\": {}, \"HOME\": {}, \"USER\": {}, \"LOGNAME\": {},\n    \"SHELL\": {}, \"PWD\": {}, \"TMPDIR\": {}, \"TZ\": {},\n\n    // Locale\n    \"LANG\": {}, \"LANGUAGE\": {},\n\n    // Terminal / color\n    \"TERM\": {}, \"TERM_PROGRAM\": {}, \"TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION\": {},\n    \"COLORTERM\": {}, \"NO_COLOR\": {}, \"FORCE_COLOR\": {},\n    \"CLICOLOR\": {}, \"CLICOLOR_FORCE\": {},\n\n    // CI detection (broad — most tools can't detect CI any other way)\n    \"CI\": {}, \"GITHUB_ACTIONS\": {}, \"GITLAB_CI\": {},\n    \"BUILDKITE\": {}, \"CIRCLECI\": {}, \"JENKINS_URL\": {},\n    \"TEAMCITY_VERSION\": {}, \"TRAVIS\": {},\n\n    // Proxies (lowercase variants too — curl/git read both)\n    \"HTTP_PROXY\": {}, \"HTTPS_PROXY\": {}, \"NO_PROXY\": {}, \"ALL_PROXY\": {},\n    \"http_proxy\": {}, \"https_proxy\": {}, \"no_proxy\": {}, \"all_proxy\": {},\n\n    // SSH agent (so plugins that fetch via git/ssh keep working)\n    \"SSH_AUTH_SOCK\": {}, \"SSH_CONNECTION\": {},\n\n    // Windows-essential\n    \"SYSTEMROOT\": {}, \"WINDIR\": {}, \"COMSPEC\": {}, \"PATHEXT\": {},\n    \"APPDATA\": {}, \"LOCALAPPDATA\": {}, \"PROGRAMDATA\": {},\n    \"PROGRAMFILES\": {}, \"PROGRAMFILES(X86)\": {},\n    \"USERPROFILE\": {}, \"USERNAME\": {}, \"HOMEDRIVE\": {}, \"HOMEPATH\": {},\n\n    // Already documented in our CLAUDE.md\n    \"ACCESSIBLE\": {},\n}\n\nvar pluginEnvPrefixes = []string{\n    \"ENTIRE_\",  // our namespace — we already inject CLI_VERSION, REPO_ROOT\n    \"LC_\",      // locale family\n    \"XDG_\",     // config-dir conventions\n}\n```\n\n## What this drops (deliberately)\n\n- **Cloud creds**: `AWS_*`, `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, `AZURE_*`\n- **Other CLI tokens**: `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GITLAB_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN`, `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- **DB DSNs**: `DATABASE_URL`, `*_DSN`\n- **Git config**: `GIT_*` — most are config but a few (`GIT_ASKPASS`, `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`) carry credential paths. Drop the whole family by default; let users opt in via `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV=GIT_*` if they have a plugin that needs it.\n- **Editor/pager**: `EDITOR`, `VISUAL`, `PAGER` — debatable; I'd start without them and add if a real plugin asks.\n\n## Escape hatches\n\n1. **`ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV`** — comma-separated names or `PREFIX_*` wildcards. Gives the user a one-line override without us having to ship a release: `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV='AWS_*,EDITOR' entire deploy ...`.\n2. **`ENTIRE_*` namespace** — for our own future contracts (auth callbacks, telemetry, repo root). Already partially done.\n3. **Future plugin manifest** — `entire-foo` could ship a sidecar declaring what it needs. Don't build this yet; revisit when a real plugin asks.\n\n## Tradeoffs to call out before shipping\n\n- **Behavior divergence from kubectl/gh.** Worth a one-paragraph note in `external-commands.md` explaining the choice (\"we filter; here's how to opt back in\"). Reviewers will ask.\n- **Plugin authors will hit this.** First time someone writes `entire-deploy` and `AWS_PROFILE` is missing, they'll be confused. Make sure the error path is good — when a plugin exits non-zero we could (separately, as a follow-up) suggest checking `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV` if their stderr mentions a missing env var. Probably overkill though.\n- **Test surface**: a single table-driven test in `plugin_test.go` covering each category (allowed exact, allowed prefix, dropped credential, opt-in via `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV`).\n\nWant me to implement this, or is this just exploring? If implementing, I'd structure it as: new `pluginEnv` function in `plugin.go`, table-driven test, and an `external-commands.md` section documenting the allowlist + escape hatch."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101759,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5722,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101759,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":5722,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101759},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamaPgsFzPY2Tkzf1z6Dr","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0d8e2ed-74c3-4650-bbb3-3133a9a61cac","timestamp":"2026-05-06T15:48:35.699Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"d3f01bb0-fb75-46a6-ae70-8aab0a703055","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/external-command-support"}
