{"parentUuid":"54eb26a2-1e1e-48e6-9632-b08cd94b640c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MubrrT2kE7gAM4Dco8d3wE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed `c6b5e5cc9`.\n\n## What landed\n\n**`cmd/entire/cli/plugin_env.go`** — `pluginEnv()` filters parent env through an exact allowlist + prefix list. `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV=\"AWS_*,GH_TOKEN\"` is the user escape hatch.\n\n**`cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go`** — `runPlugin` now calls `pluginEnv(os.Environ(), extras...)` instead of appending to the full parent env.\n\n**Tests** — table-driven unit tests for every category (allowed, dropped, prefix, override exact, override wildcard, whitespace handling, malformed entries, extras-override-parent), plus two integration tests that exercise the real binary end-to-end.\n\n**Docs** — `docs/architecture/external-commands.md` now has an \"Environment filtering\" section explaining what's forwarded, why we diverge from kubectl/gh, and the `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV` opt-in syntax.\n\n## Notes worth flagging before review\n\n- **Behavior change**: any third-party plugin currently relying on inheriting `AWS_*`, `EDITOR`, `GIT_*`, etc., will break and its author needs to either be on the allowlist or document `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_ENV`. Worth calling out in changelog when this ships.\n- **`__complete`** (cobra's hidden completion command) is still a theoretical name collision with `entire-__complete` on PATH — out of scope here, since `__complete` isn't typed by users.\n- **Future**: if/when `ENTIRE_AUTH_TOKEN` exists, the gh-style **pull pattern** (plugin calls `entire auth token`) is a better fit than push, and would build cleanly on top of this — we'd just inject `ENTIRE_PATH=os.Args[0]` so the plugin can find the parent binary."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":162254,"output_tokens":653,"server_tool_use":{"web_search